Part 5 — Permanent Delete

Recommended endpoint

DELETE /workspaces/{workspaceId}/areas/{areaId}/permanent

This follows the existing REST convention (resource sub-action as a path suffix). DELETE is semantically correct. Alternatives like POST .../purge diverge from the established HTTP method convention used in the rest of the API.

Preconditions

1. Workspace must exist (same workspaceRepository.findById check as all area endpoints)
2. Area must exist (areaRepository.findById → AreaNotFoundException if not found)
3. Area must belong to the workspace (same cross-check as existing endpoints → AreaNotFoundException)
4. Area must have status == DELETED → if ACTIVE, return 409 AREA_NOT_DELETED (new exception + error code)

No expectedVersion OCC is needed for permanent delete. The status == DELETED guard is sufficient: if the area was restored between the client seeing it as DELETED and submitting the permanent delete, it will be ACTIVE and the call is rejected with 409. This is consistent and predictable without adding OCC.

