Part 8 — Audit semantics

Current DESIGN.md (Section "Audit Trail") states:

▎ "AreaVersion is the persistent audit trail for Area Mutations. It combines two responsibilities in a single append-only record."

and

▎ "AreaVersion is append-only. Existing AreaVersion records are not modified."

These statements need a bounded qualification. With permanent deletion:

- While an Area exists: AreaVersion is append-only. Records are never modified or deleted.
- Permanent deletion: an explicit user action that physically removes both the Area row and all its associated AreaVersion rows. After permanent deletion, no records remain for that Area.

DESIGN.md must be updated to state:

▎ "AreaVersion is append-only for retained Areas. Explicit permanent deletion by the user physically removes both the Area row and all its associated AreaVersion rows. The audit trail is therefore scoped to Areas that have not been permanently deleted."

This is not a contradiction — it is a bounded guarantee. The word "immutable" as applied to individual AreaVersion records remains correct (no AreaVersion row is ever modified), but the guarantee that records are never deleted must be dropped in favor of the narrower scoped statement.

