No PURGED change type or status should be added.

Rationale: a hypothetical PURGED AreaVersion entry would be created immediately before permanent deletion, then deleted in the same transaction. It would never be visible to any query. Its only purpose would be to satisfy metrics or observability, but a separate metric counter (area.permanent.deletions.total) achieves that without schema changes. The chk_area_version_change_type CHECK constraint would require a migration to add PURGED, and the AreaMetricsListener would need updating to recognize it. None of this is warranted.

